{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% import "macros.html.j2" as m %}
{% block title %}Rules{% endblock %}
{% block toc %}
{{ m.toc_item("invariants", "Hard-coded limits", "code") }}
{{ m.toc_item("rules", "Risk rules", "risk") }}
{% endblock %}
{% block main %}
<header class="hero">
  <p class="eyebrow">Rules</p>
  <h1>The numbers the council cannot change</h1>
  <p class="lede">Prompts explain these rules to the models; code enforces them. A change to any number is a policy change, recorded in every sealed run by the policy file's hash.</p>
</header>

{% call m.section("invariants", 1, "Hard-coded limits", "code") %}
<p>These are constants in the code. The policy file may be stricter, never looser, and a test enforces it.</p>
<ul class="ticks">
  <li>Total exposure at most <span class="n">{{ invariants.gross }}x</span> the portfolio.</li>
  <li>Kill switch, measured from the best value ever reached: {{ kill_phrase }}. Whatever the policy file says, code stops at a fall of <span class="n">{{ ((1 - invariants.halt) * 100) | round(0) | int }}%</span> at the latest.</li>
  <li>Stop-loss on every opening order: <strong>{{ "required" if invariants.stop else "not required" }}</strong>.</li>
  <li>Human approval of every order: <strong>{{ "required" if invariants.human else "not required" }}</strong>.</li>
  <li>Only the dedicated agent portfolio is ever touched: <strong>{{ "yes" if invariants.main_account else "no" }}</strong>.</li>
</ul>
{% endcall %}

{% call m.section("rules", 2, "Risk rules", "risk") %}
<p>Every rule the risk engine checks on every run. <em>x</em> means a multiple of the portfolio's value (0.5x = half of it).</p>
{{ m.wrap_open("Risk rules") }}
<table class="rules wide stack" role="table">
  <thead><tr role="row"><th role="columnheader">Rule</th><th role="columnheader">In plain words</th><th role="columnheader">What it is</th><th role="columnheader">Numbers</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for r in rules %}
  <tr role="row">
    <td role="cell" class="n"><strong>{{ r.rule_id or "—" }}</strong></td>
    <td role="cell" class="text">{{ r.plain or r.title }}</td>
    <td role="cell" class="text" data-label="What it is">{{ r.title }}<br><code class="muted small">{{ r.key }}</code></td>
    <td role="cell" class="numbers text" data-label="Numbers">{% for k, v in r.numbers %}<span class="kv"><span class="k">{{ k }}</span> <span class="n">{{ v }}</span></span>{% endfor %}</td>
  </tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p class="muted small">Source: <code>policy/risk.yaml</code>. Its hash is recorded in every sealed run.</p>
{% endcall %}
{% endblock %}
